title: The measured bill, read from Cost Management
subtitle: week-12-detections-as-code — ActualCost, 2026-11-01 to 2026-11-12
width: 1000
---
$ az rest --method post --url ".../Microsoft.CostManagement/query?api-version=2023-03-01" \
    --body @query.json      # ActualCost, grouped by ServiceName

  (no rows)

  TOTAL: 0.00 USD

# A zero result is not a fact until the method is proved. The same query over
# October, when week 11 ran, returns:
#
#        6.0000 USD  Azure Grafana Service
#        1.0839 USD  Virtual Machines
#        0.0618 USD  Virtual Network
#        0.0345 USD  Storage
#        0.0202 USD  Container Registry
#        0.0121 USD  Azure Monitor
#     TOTAL 7.2125
#
# So the query works, and November is empty because nothing was billable --
# not because the question was asked wrongly.
